{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #291: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $n\\geq 1$ and define $L_n$ to be the least common multiple of $\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$ and $a_n$ by\\[\\sum_{1\\leq k\\leq n}\\frac{1}{k}=\\frac{a_n}{L_n}.\\]Is it true that $(a_n,L_n)=1$ and $(a_n,L_n)>1$ both occur for infinitely many $n$? Current best: There is in fact a necessary and sufficient condition: a prime $p\\leq n$ divides $(a_n,L_n)$ if and only if $p$ divides the numerator of $1+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{k}$, where $k$ is the leading digit of $n$ in base $p$. Prize: no. OEIS: A110566. Tags: number theory, unit fractions."},"claim_id":"vcl_0eb3129e5f58ce17c48624deab677fa3c2a0e451c42b143c1a1d5777b3226776","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:291","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_3b9cd542fd44ba79","object_root":"sha256:1eb2be26a06ec740b6e73c600c9c84c20fe213b6dd5dc5b2062455798de16e3d","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:29